# azure-bundle.manifest — the logical secret names sealed into the
# PRODUCTION Azure bootstrap bundle. This is the checked-in shadow of an
# immutable Key Vault secret (tr-bootstrap-wrap in trquillkv): CI can read
# it, the live bundle it mirrors it cannot.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. deploy-azure-aci.sh names a QUILL_*_SECRET for every
# provider. The sealed bundle contains a value for each NAME below. When the
# deploy names a secret the bundle lacks, the enclave dies at bootstrap with
# "no entry ... in the bundle" AFTER a full attestation round trip -- it took
# Dubai down on 2026-08-24 (stepfun + 18 more), the Foundry crash on 08-23,
# and NVIDIA NIM was one rebase away from being the next. test_azure_bundle_
# manifest.py fails CI when the deploy demands a name absent here, so that
# drift is caught at merge instead of at an enclave's death.
#
# DO NOT hand-edit. azure-seal-bundle.py --upload-secret rewrites it from the
# bundle it just sealed. To add a provider on Azure: provision its key, seal
# a new bundle (which regenerates this file and prints a new version), pin the
# new QUILL_AZURE_BUNDLE_VERSION, and commit this file in the same change.
#
# bundle-version: 6cc3b63be84147839b85c7dcd0cbd8a9
